			"Message": "refactor(Mountain): Align extension IPC handlers with PascalCase invocation\n\nUpdate `ExtensionInstall` and `ExtensionUninstall` handlers in the Wind IPC service layer to strictly follow the project's PascalCase naming convention for method calls.\n\nReplace direct function-style invocations of `NowNano` (`crate::IPC::DevLog::NowNano()`) with explicit static method syntax (`crate::IPC::DevLog::NowNano::Fn()`). This aligns with the modularized `DevLog` crate architecture and the 'one export per file' pattern where utility functions are exposed as static methods on their respective structs.\n\nThis change ensures consistency with recent IPC refactorings (navigation, performance, and security modules) and maintains the native backend's adherence to Rust idiom requirements for the Mountain crate.",
			"SHA": "769e6c2942fb09b888ae83a29d5756c01e54e51c"
		}
